[ceiling] The two pump-cartridge pull roofs share the neighboring tee-carrier grips' Z=217.245 roof plane because each hand squeezes those two faces as one motion. They remain broad, flat contact faces through the complete fingertip depth; pitching either roof into a corbel would make the paired grip surfaces disagree. The production slice gives each roof one bed-rooted tree with one interface, directly removable through the open side pocket.
